{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "refactor",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The architecture registry had an unsorted model list, and Gemma3's preprocessing comment omitted the batch dimension already added by the code.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_732ff72aa40b48c2910befdd064d5f4d", "call_caa349a585294dba927bce2ef02b2f1e"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "The cleanup reorders existing imports and registry entries without adding or removing models. The Gemma3 edit corrects documentation rather than changing tensor construction.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_732ff72aa40b48c2910befdd064d5f4d", "call_caa349a585294dba927bce2ef02b2f1e"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "Registry iteration order changes, but the inspected configuration loader selects entries by architecture string, not position. The declared architecture strings are distinct, so the reorder does not introduce a duplicate-key overwrite.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_553297f1cb284dabbb4299879518f635", "call_95b45d933afc48efb2af48eecbe4faea", "call_637f21c56cf44f82b08be112ae235eae"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "The Gemma3 vision introduction entry establishes that preprocessing already produced a half-precision tensor with a leading batch dimension. The Mistral3 introduction entry establishes the registry addition retained by this cleanup.",
      "basis": "ancestor",
      "evidence": ["call_ce4dd66a2d484f72b79ab24b4f4bfe13", "call_70d307b07126468daaa77fd8fc8804bf"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Issue #7, “quantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,” reports a native-extension import failure and a reporter-provided environment workaround. Its connection to this inspection is only an inferred shared config.py path; it does not establish a problem addressed by this cleanup.",
      "basis": "inference",
      "evidence": ["call_2dbc435199dd444c8089931f1cd037e0", "call_95b45d933afc48efb2af48eecbe4faea"]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Import-order side effects and model execution were not tested.",
    "No numerical algorithm changes here warrant a scalar computation; tensor-shape reasoning is source inspection, not execution."
  ],
  "links": [
    "532d78658414d8f9aabce52cb64b982b3ec53388",
    "45fa5abff9001ff373a612303e48ec01d34efe42"
  ],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "models",
      "title": "Registry ordering and Gemma3 shape documentation",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "ARCHITECTURES still maps each model's config_class.arch_string to its architecture string, configuration class and model class. get_architectures returns that dictionary unchanged; the only discovered repository caller retrieves a configuration class by the checkpoint's architecture name.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_553297f1cb284dabbb4299879518f635", "call_ebdc3247e53c4e6d9a3d48e636966aa8", "call_95b45d933afc48efb2af48eecbe4faea"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Gemma3 preprocessing transposes an RGB image from height-width-channel order to channel-height-width order, then converts it to half precision and applies unsqueeze(0). The corrected comment therefore describes (1, 3, resized_height, resized_width): one batch item and three color channels. The existing load-shape hook likewise supplies a leading singleton batch, while get_image_embeddings removes that dimension after forwarding.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_d432a64409014bd89e62344d4d3a3d95", "call_caa349a585294dba927bce2ef02b2f1e"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Reorders architecture imports and registration entries, and corrects Gemma3's preprocessing shape comment without changing tensor operations."
}
